# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRIVATE LANGUAGE DATA — never commit a real OneStory project.
#
# A .onestory file is a translation team's live corpus. It carries member names,
# email addresses and stored HgPassword values alongside years of unpublished
# language data. One was committed here under sample/ and had to be purged from
# the entire history on 2026-08-13 — force-pushing every branch and every tag,
# which broke every clone in existence.
#
# Keeping a real project LOCALLY, for reference and testing, is expected and
# fine — that is exactly what these rules are for. Drop it in sample/ and git
# will not see it. Do not defeat them with `git add -f`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: it must be `/sample/*`, not `/sample/`. Git does not descend into an
# excluded DIRECTORY, so a `!` negation cannot rescue a file inside one — with
# `/sample/` the README below is silently ignored too, and the folder vanishes
# from the repo along with the explanation of why it is empty.
*.onestory
/sample/*
!/sample/README.md

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Rust / Tauri build artifacts
src-tauri/target/

# Generated mobile icons (desktop-only project — only desktop icons are committed)
src-tauri/icons/android/
src-tauri/icons/ios/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editor
.vscode/
settings.json

# Misc
out/
dist/
package.json.txt
